   tree. First, the root bridge is identiﬁed as the bridge with the least serial number. Next, the root sends out (one or
  more) data units to enable the setting up of the spanning tree of shortest paths from the root bridge to each bridge.

  Each bridge identiﬁes a port (the root port) through which it will forward frames to the root bridge. Port conﬂicts are
  always resolved in favour of the port with the lower index value. When there is a possibility of multiple bridges
  forwarding to the same LAN (but not through the root port), ties are broken as follows: bridges closest to the root
  get preference and between such bridges, the one with the lowest serial number is preferred.
 For the given connection of LANs by bridges, which one of the following choices represents the depth ﬁrst traversal
 of the spanning tree of bridges?', '{"A": "B.", "C": "D."}', 'A', 0, 1, 'gatecse-2006,computer-networks,bridges,normal', 1, 'filter1_vol3.pdf', 114);
